th i really  have to recommend you must see it is  this one okay so now that we've set the  right mood how likely is it that we will  even go to elbaf in the first place  after all it hasn't been officially  confirmed at all if we're actually going  to go there and author either oda has to  keep pushing back his goal for finishing  one piece as it is so the only way for  an albert arc to exist is if it heavily  contributes to the climax of the series  pushes the story and its development  further and has a clear connection to  wano and for full disclosure it is of  course absolutely possible that elbaf  will be skipped or just be referenced in  passing biota as well now being said  there is a really good reason why me and  large parts of the fandom find that  possibility unlikely and basically take  a visit to elbaf for granted it has been  foreshadowed as far back as chapter 115  when the straw has arrived on little  garden on little garland little garden  where they met the giant story and  braggy  there are so many important character  arcs that are all bound to culminate  into elbaf at the center of it all is  undoubtedly usopp i've just recently  made a full video on usopp's character  development and why i think elbaf will  be his big arc so if you haven't seen it  already i strongly recommend that you  check that one out afterwards but all  you have to know for now is that usop  has been forging relationships and  friendships with the giants of elba  throughout the story where he has gained  their respect and loyalty and on more  than one occasion has promised to go to  albath one day to become a brave warrior  of the sea like his giant friends  [Music]  and don't worry i'll be telling you what  i believe will happen with usopp in just  a little bit the other character that  has major connections to the giants is  of course none other than the empress  herself big mom who not only grew up on  elbaf but who also has a crazy obsession  with integrating the giants into her  ideal world even though the giants  despise her for her actions as a child  but surprisingly enough big mom isn't  the only emperor with ties to this  islands in my character analysis on  shanks i explored the strong ties shanks  has to nordic mythology in fact not only  does he sail on a viking ship but his  entire character seems to be inspired by  the nordic god tear and in that same  video i explored the idea that elbaf  might be in fact under the protection of  the red hair pirates and zen zuano will  be the arc where luffy will finally rise  into the ranks of the yonko i think it's  about time that he met his mentor again  now that he's become the great pirate  that shanks wanted him to be  and aside from all these character arcs  it seems like albath might be home to  the father tree atom from which what the  thousand sunny was made as well it has  been speculated that this tree might be  the main entrance to the sky islands but  honestly no matter what it will turn out  to be it will play some important role  in the lore of the story should it  actually be there and if you watch  really carefully in the next clip you  can see something that looks  suspiciously like a giant tree trunk in  the back  and uh this might be a bit of a stupid  argument maybe but if oda had planned to  skip going to albev altogether he surely  would have shown it off to us in all its  glory instead of shrouding it in so much  mystery and barely giving us a glimpse  of its shoreline oh and we have this  pretty telling color spread of the straw  hats as vikings so with all that being  said i now want to share with you my  timeline of the things that could and in  my opinion should happen during the  albert arc and while i base all of this  on everything that has been foreshadowed  in the story keep in mind that i could  be completely wrong about this that  being said i do believe that there is a  pretty good chance a good chunk of this  will happen in some way or form so 